.TH "VISUALVIEWPORT.RESIZE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VisualViewport.resize_event \- VisualViewport: resize event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]resize\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]VisualViewport\f[R]
interface is fired when the visual viewport is resized.
This allows you to position elements relative to the visual viewport as
it is zoomed, which would normally be anchored to the layout viewport.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqresize\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onresize = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See the \f[CR]VisualViewport\f[R] landing page for a usage demo.
